{
  "summary": "This study investigates a monolithic thin-film lithium niobate platform integrating nonlinear frequency conversion and high-speed electro-optic switching for quantum defect manipulation. The approach combines periodically poled frequency conversion with GHz-bandwidth electro-opt. switching to generate milliwatt-scale green light with 42.2 dB extinction ratio. Results enable coherent spin control and time-resolved lifetime measurements of nitrogen-vacancy centers via nanosecond gating, demonstrating a scalable framework for quantum communication nodes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Monolithic thin-film lithium niobate platform integrates nonlinear frequency conversion and GHz-bandwidth electro-optic switching",
    "Device delivers over 1 mW green-light power with 42.2 dB extinction ratio",
    "Enables coherent spin control and time-resolved lifetime measurements of nitrogen-vacancy centers"
  ],
  "study_type": "Monolithic thin-film lithium niobate platform with integrated nonlinear frequency conversion and electro-optic switching",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable platform for high-rate quantum communication nodes by unifying milliwatt-scale visible light generation with high-speed active manipulation of solid-state quantum defects."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a biomimetic CF/PEEK scaffold with a nano-heterojunction to enhance vascularized bone regeneration in large segmental load-bearing defects. The scaffold utilizes endogenous electric fields to regulate functional ions (Ca2+, Cu2+, Mg2+), improving osteogenic and angiogenic differentiation via EGFR-PI3K/Akt signaling. In vivo results show superior bone and vascular repair under mechanical stress, enabling rapid vascularized regeneration in complex load-bearing conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The biomimetic scaffold enhances vascularized bone regeneration in large segment. segmental load-bearing bone defects through endogenous ion regulation.",
    "The scaffold promotes osteogenic and angiogenic differentiation via EGFR-PI3K/Akt signaling pathway.",
    "In vivo models confirm superior bone and vascular repair capacity under mechanical stress conditions."
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo and in vitro studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a novel strategy for repairing load-bearing large segmental bone defects using bioelectric field-guided biomimetic materials, advancing understanding of ion-mediated vascularized bone regeneration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies a pseudoenzyme T6P synthase (TPS-II) as a direct sensor of trehalose-6-phosphate (T6P) in plants. T6P binding induces conformational changes that repress SnRK1, a key metabolic regulator. Loss of TPS-II activates stress responses and catabolic pathways, indicating T6P's role in balancing carbon metabolism. The mechanism is conserved across plants, revealing a fundamental pathway for carbon availability signaling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TPS-II acts as a T6P sensor by undergoing conformational changes upon T6P binding",
    "T6P binding represses SnRK1 kinase activity to regulate metabolic pathways",
    "TPS-II loss activates stress responses and suppresses anabolic gene expression"
  ],
  "study_type": "Functional and chemical biology approaches",
  "scientific_significance": "This work elucidates a conserved mechanism for coupling carbon availability to metabolic homeostasis in plants, resolving longstanding questions about sugar signaling."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the kinetic limitations in conversion-type sodium-ion battery anodes by introducing a spin-polarization-engineered antibonding-orbital modulation approach. Magnetic doping induces spin-state transitions that enhance electron occupation in antibonding orbitals, strengthening metal-chalcogen bonds. The Mn-FeS2/CoS2 anode achieves ultrahigh-rate performance (300 mA h g-1 at 120 A g-1) and exceptional cycling stability (100% retention after 13,000 cycles).",
  "key_findings": [
    "Magnetic manganese doping triggers a spin-state transition from low-spin to high-spin configurations",
    "Enhanced electron occupation in antibonding orbitals strengthens metal-chalcogen bonds",
    "Mn-FeS2/CoS2 anode demonstrates ultrahigh-rate capability (300 mA h g-1 at 120 A g-1) and 100% retention over 13,000 cycles"
  ],
  "study_type": "Proof of concept with magnetic heteroatom doping",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a universal strategy for accelerating reaction kinetics in conversion-type anodes by manipulating spin states to regulate bond strength, offering a pathway to overcome intrinsic kinetic barriers in sodium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a self-assembled hydrophobic polymer nanoplatform (Tri@N) for targeted membrane protein degradation and immunomodulatory drug delivery. The platform utilizes intracellular GSH-triggered disassembly to expose hydrophobic tags that degrade EGFR via proteasomal and autophagy-lysosomal pathways while releasing niclosamide to inhibit STAT3/PD-L1 signaling. In colorectal cancer models, Tri@N enhanced CD8+ T cell activity and tumor suppression through coordinated EGFR degradation and PD-L1 downregulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Tri@N degrades EGFR via proteasomal and autophagy-lysosomal pathways using hydrophobic polymer tags",
    "Niclosamide release suppresses STAT3/PD-L1 signaling to modulate immune responses",
    "Tri@N achieves tumor suppression in colorectal cancer models through enhanced CD8+ T cell activity"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo colorectal cancer models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a dual-functional nanoplatform that integrates targeted protein degradation with immunomodulatory drug delivery, advancing strategies for multimodal cancer therapy through coordinated membrane protein clearance and immune activation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how maternal milk glycoprotein osteopontin regulates neonatal hematopoiesis by shaping the microbiome. The research demonstrates osteopontin's role in promoting dendritic cell development and reducing severe respiratory infections through a maternal milk-microbiota pathway. These findings link early nutrition to immune development and long-term disease susceptibility.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Osteop:promotes dendritic cell development",
    "Osteopontin shapes neonatal microbiome to regulate hematopoiesis",
    "Osteopontin reduces severe respiratory infections via maternal milk-microbiota pathway"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a maternal milk-microbiota pathway that connects early nutrition with immune development and long-term disease susceptibility, providing mechanistic insight into how neonatal hematopoiesis is influenced by early-life microbial exposure."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates sustainable recycling of rare-earth permanent magnet (REPM) machining swarf using hydrogen plasma reduction (HPR). The approach involves tuning hydrogen content and treatment time to separate metallic iron and a Nd2O3-rich rare-earth fraction, enabling direct rare-earth hydride formation. The process achieves high-purity feedstock without acid use, reducing CO2 emissions by up to 70 kg CO2-eq per kg compared to conventional REPM production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Hydrogen plasma reduction separates metallic iron and Nd2:O3-rich rare-earth fractions from REPM swarf",
    "The method enables direct rare-earth hydride formation in molten state",
    "The process reduces CO2 emissions by up to 70 kg CO2-eq per kg of REPM compared to conventional production"
  ],
  "study_type": "Hydrogen plasma reduction (HPR) process",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a scalable pathway for sustainable rare-earth recycling, significantly lowering the carbon footprint of permanent magnet production while enhancing resource efficiency without chemical reagents."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates how biomaterials regulate macrophage polarization in bone tissue engineering by integrating interface sensing with immune microenvironment remodeling. It proposes a four-dimensional framework linking material properties to intracellular mechanisms like mitochondrial reprogramming and ncRNA networks. The study emphasizes bidirectional feedback loops between material systems and cellular responses to achieve osteoimmune balance, highlighting potential for programmable biomaterials in bone repair.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Material interfaces activate and integrate bioactive signals to influence macrophage polarization states",
    "Intracellular mechanisms including mitochondrial reprogramming and ncRNA networks modulate immune responses",
    "Bidirectional feedback loops between material systems and cellular machinery enable adaptive immune microenvironment remodeling"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a conceptual framework for designing biomaterials that dynamically regulate osteoimmune responses, advancing the field toward programmable immune modulation for enhanced bone regeneration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates why deep subcortical brain regions, such as the hypothalamus and brainstem, exhibit greater neuronal diversity than cortical areas despite having fewer neurons. Using whole-brain cell atlases, it proposes a dual subsystem model: a 'learning subsystem' (cortex, striatum, cerebellum) scales through repetitive module replication, while a 'steering subsystem' (hypothalamus, pallidum, brainstem) diversifies cell types for innate behaviors. This framework explains evolutionary divergence in brain architecture and potential implications for neurobiology and AI model design.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Deep subcortical structures have higher neuronal diversity than cortical regions despite lower neuron counts",
    "Learning subsystem scales via repetitive module replication to maximize computational capacity",
    "Steering subsystem diversifies cell types to encode innate drives and reflexes"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This framework provides a unified explanation for evolutionary divergence in brain architecture and offers insights into neurobiological mechanisms underlying brain disease and artificial intelligence model design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a dual-modal neural fiber that integrates touch sensing and in-sensor computing to improve human-machine interfaces. The researchers developed an ultrarobust material capable of detecting position (<5 mm) and pressure (0.6 N) with high reliability under bending and load. The fiber achieves 98.21% accuracy in intention recognition through synchronized feature fusion, demonstrating significant potential for next-generation wearable interfaces.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Unprecedented position resolution of <5 mm and pressure detection limit of 0.6 N",
    "300 times load-bearing capacity with <8% performance fluctuation under bending",
    "98.21% accuracy in intention recognition via in-sensor computing"
  ],
  "study_type": "In-sensor computing dual-modal neural fiber",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a unified material-architecture paradigm for ultrarobust, dual-modal sensing with in-sensor computing, advancing wearable human-machine interfaces through enhanced information density and real-time feature fusion."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how dynamic tensile stretching of mesenchymal stem cell-laden auxetic scaffolds enhances YAP-dependent miR-30 enrichment in extracellular vesicles for pulmonary fibrosis therapy. Using a photo-crosslinkable lung decellularized matrix with auxetic scaffolds, MSCs were subjected to cyclic stretching mimicking lung motion. The resulting dynamically conditioned EVs significantly reduced fibrosis markers in vivo and exhibited dual mechanisms: inhibiting myofibroblast activation and promoting macrophage polarization via miR-30.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dynamic tensile stretching on auxetic scaffolds increased YAP nuclear accumulation and miR-30 enrichment in MSC-derived EVs",
    "dEVs suppressed myofibroblast activation and induced M2 macrophage polarization through miR-30",
    "dEVs restored mitochondrial function and attenuated collagen deposition in bleomycin-induced pulmonary fibrosis"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo model using photo-crosslinkable lung decellularized extracellular matrix with auxetic scaffolds",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes mechanical priming as a strategy to engineer EVs with specific therapeutic cargo for pulmonary fibrosis, highlighting the YAP/miR-30 axis and mitochondrial restoration as critical targets for tissue repair."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of measuring somatic genomic variation across human cells. Using the SMaHT Network's tools, it generated the first comprehensive body-wide map of somatic mosaicism. The findings establish a baseline 'normal' variation profile, enabling future research into how this variation influences development, aging, and disease processes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "First comprehensive body-wide map of somatic mosaicism",
    "Establishment of a baseline 'normal' somatic variation profile",
    "Foundation for studying somatic variation's role in development, aging, and disease"
  ],
  "study_type": "SMaHT Network benchmarked tools",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides the first systematic framework for quantifying and understanding human somatic genomic diversity, enabling precise investigations into its functional impacts across biological processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates overcoming the activity-stability trade-off in iridium-free acidic oxygen evolution reactions (OER) by engineering lutetium-stabilized cobalt oxide catalysts. Using site-specific electronic modulation, the catalyst achieves enhanced OER activity and stability in proton exchange membrane water electrolyzers. Operando spectroscopy and simulations show Lu incorporation strengthens Co-O bonds and suppresses dissolution, enabling durable operation at industrially relevant current densities and extended stability beyond 900 hours.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Lu0.08Co2.92O4 catalyst achieves 1000 mA cm-2 current density at 1.837 V in acidic OER",
    "Lu incorporation suppresses Co2+ dissolution through strengthened Co-O covalency and robust Lu-O bonds",
    "The catalyst maintains stable operation for over 900 hours under stepwise current density changes"
  ],
  "study_type": "Operando spectroscopy and theoretical simulations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a structural strategy to simultaneously enhance activity and durability in acidic OER catalysts, addressing a fundamental challenge in sustainable hydrogen production without noble metals."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a nanoregulatory strategy to disrupt the iron-ROS cycle in Parkinson's disease by engineering nitrogen-doped carbon dots with electronic properties that enable iron chelation and ROS regulation. The nanoregulators achieved brain delivery, reduced iron deposition, preserved dopaminergic neurons, and improved motor function in Parkinsonian mice, demonstrating disease-modifying effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nitrogen-doped carbon dots engineered to regulate iron-ROS cycle via electronic structure",
    "LRP1-mediated brain delivery and cerebrospinal fluid clearance of nanoregulators",
    "Reduced iron deposition, preserved dopaminergic neurons, and improved motor function in Parkinsonian mice"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo studies",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a targeted mechanism for interrupting iron-:ROS pathological cycles in Parkinson's disease, offering a novel therapeutic strategy that addresses root causes rather than symptom management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study benchmarks somatic mutation detection methods using the SMaHT Network. It evaluates sequencing technologies, computational approaches, and experimental designs across cell lines and donor tissues, generating >1,00.000× short-read and 100-400× long-read data. Key findings include improved mutation calling with donor-specific and pangenome-inferred diploid assemblies, single-cell sequencing resolving cell-type-specific heterogeneity, and the complementary utility of bulk, single-cell, and duplex analyses for comprehensive mosaicism characterization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Donor-specific and pangenome-inferred diploid assemblies enhance mutation calling accuracy",
    "Single-cell sequencing identifies cell-type-specific mutational heterogeneity",
    "Bulk, single-cell, and duplex analyses collectively provide comprehensive mosaicism characterization"
  ],
  "study_type": "Benchmarking experiments with cell lines and donor tissues",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes standardized methodologies for accurate somatic mutation detection across diverse genomic regions, advancing the clinical and research applications of mosaicism analysis in human biology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates magnetic-field-annealing (MFA) in high-entropy alloys to optimize microwave absorbers for 5G/6G applications. By applying MFA at 0.5 T to FeCoNiCr composites, researchers achieved a reflection loss minimum of -72.30 dB at .59 mm and a 4.40 GHz absorption bandwidth. The material retained 92.7% of its bandwidth at 85°C, indicating robust thermal stability. Atomic-scale analysis linked this response to Co-centered short-range order.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MFA at 0.5 T in FeCoNiCr alloys achieved a reflection loss minimum of -72.30 dB at 1.59 mm",
    "Maximum effective absorption bandwidth of 4.40 GHz at room temperature, retaining 92.7% of bandwidth at 85°C",
    "Co-centered short-range order explains the electromagnetic response through atomic-scale mechanisms"
  ],
  "study_type": "Magnetic field annealing (MFA) of high-entropy alloys",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes magnetic-field-annealing as a strategy to engineer short-range order in high-entropy alloys, enhancing microwave absorption properties while maintaining thermal stability for next-generation communication technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates an ultrasound-triggered electroactive hydrogel for spinal cord injury repair. The hydrogel integrates conductive MXene nanosheets into a silk fibroin/tannic acid matrix, enabling tissue-matched mechanics, electrical conductivity, and stimulus-responsive output. Upon ultrasound activation, it promotes autophagy via JNK signaling, reduces inflammation, enhances remyelination, and improves functional recovery in rat models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ultrasound activation of the hydrogel generates localized bioelectrical cues at the injury site",
    "The hydrogel enhances autophagic flux through Ca2+-dependent JNK signaling",
    "SMT + ultrasound treatment improved neural repair, remyelination, and functional outcomes in SCI rats"
  ],
  "study_type": "Rat model of spinal cord injury",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a remotely activatable biomaterial that integrates dynamic bioelectrical modulation with mechanical support for spinal cord repair, advancing strategies for targeted neural regeneration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how somatic epimutations influence chromatin accessibility in diploid human cells. Using Fiber-seq inferred regulatory elements (FIRE), the researchers mapped accessible chromatin across the 6 Gbp genome, identifying haplotype-selective chromatin accessibility (HSCA). They found HSCA at the HLA locus in immune cells, disrupted transcription factor binding near disease variants, and autosomal somatic epimutations that propagate clonally to create mitotically stable chromatin alterations beyond genetic determinism.",
  "key_findings": [
    "FIRE provides a comprehensive quantitative map of accessible chromatin across the diploid human genome",
    "Haplotype-selective chromatin accessibility (HSCA) was detected at the HLA locus in immune cells",
    "Autosomal somatic chromatin epimutations propagate clonally to create mitotically stable non-genetically deterministic alterations"
  ],
  "study_type": "Fiber-seq inferred regulatory elements (FIRE)",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that somatic epimutations can create mitotically stable chromatin alterations independent of genetic determinism, revealing a layer of epigenetic regulation that contributes to cellular diversity and disease susceptibility."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses urgent needs for polymer materials that integrate flame retardancy, UV resistance, and antibacterial properties. Using a single biguanide unit chemically bonded to the polymer chain, the researchers achieved UL-94 V-0 flame retardancy, ≥99.3% UV shielding, and ≥99.0% antibacterial efficacy. The approach provides a unified strategy for triple protection without additive migration risks.",
  "key_findings": [
    "UL-94 V-0 flame retardancy",
    "≥99.3% UV light shielding",
    "≥99.0% antibacterial activity"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a single molecular unit enabling simultaneous integration of three critical safety properties in polymers, advancing materials design for multi-threat protection without traditional additive limitations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how catalytic MXene coatings can reprogram radiation-induced foreign body response to prevent capsular contracture in silicone implants. Using a murine irradiation model, researchers engineered Ti3C2Tx MXene-modified PDMS (APM) to modulate interfacial redox activity. Results showed reduced inflammation, lower collagen deposition, and preserved microvasculature in irradiated implants compared to controls.",
  "key_findings": [
    "APM-coated implants preserved CD31+/ICAM-1-low microvasculature in irradiated tissue",
    "Significant reduction in peri-implant pro-inflammatory macrophage accumulation",
    "Decreased capsular thickness and collagen deposition in irradiated implants"
  ],
  "study_type": "Murine peri-implant irradiation model",
  "scientific_significance": "MXene-based catalytic coatings provide a mechanistic strategy to disrupt radiation-fibrosis crosstalk, offering a potential solution for radiation-exposed implant complications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates somatic mutation patterns in cancer genomes using near-telomere-to-telomere sequencing. It identifies 16% of somatic variants in regions absent from standard references, with satellite repeats as UV-induced mutation hotspots. Centromere kinetochore regions show aneuploidy breakpoints and genetic variation, while epigenetic changes are cancer-specific. The research reveals telomere dynamics and epimutations during tumor evolution, providing a framework for studying human mosaicism.",
  "key_findings": [
    "16% of somatic variants localize to sequences absent from GRCh38",
    "Satellite repeats act as hotspots for UV-associated mutagenesis",
    "Centromere kinetochore regions are focal sites of aneuploidy breakpoints and somatic genetic variation"
  ],
  "study_type": "near-telomere-to-telomere diploid assembly with deep sequencing",
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes a comprehensive framework for analyzing previously inaccessible genomic regions in human mosaicism, advancing understanding of somatic variation mechanisms in cancer and non-cancerous tissues."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates achieving ordered crystallographic orientation in Dion-Jacobson 2D perovskites to enhance solar cell stability. Using a two-step processing method with Ruddlesden-Popper phase 2D perovskites, the researchers created oriented films that improved photovoltaic efficiency to 21.1% and maintained 98.1% efficiency after 2000 hours at 65°C under continuous illumination.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ordered crystallographic orientation of Dion-Jacobson 2D perovskites via Ruddlesden-Popper phase modification",
    "Solar cells achieved 21.1% efficiency with 98.1% retention after 2000 hours at 65°C under ISOS-L-2 conditions",
    "The strategy is applicable across various organic diammonium-based Dion-Jacobson 2D perovskites"
  ],
  "study_type": "Two-step processing method with Ruddlesden-Popper phase 2D perovskites",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a method to achieve oriented crystallographic alignment in Dion-Jacobson 2D perovskites, addressing a critical stability challenge in high-efficiency photovoltaic devices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a blood-transforming coating strategy to enhance hemostasis and vascularized bone regeneration. The engineered GM/TCP@PEG microspheres crosslink with blood components to form a hydrogel, improving clotting efficiency, shear strength, and vascularization. In vivo, it achieved rapid hemostasis and accelerated bone repair in hemorrhagic models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "GM/TCP@PEG microspheres crosslink with blood to form a hydrogel enhancing hemostasis",
    "The coating significantly improved clotting efficiency and shear strength compared to controls",
    "In vivo, it enabled rapid hemostasis and accelerated bone regeneration in hemorrhagic models"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo experiments with animal models",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach transforms blood from a barrier to a functional component, providing a novel mechanism for hemostasis and tissue regeneration in hemorrhagic environments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used spatial transcriptomics to analyze Medicago nodules across developmental stages, revealing coordinated host-rhizobial gene expression patterns. It identified two transcription factors essential for nodule meristem maintenance and linked ROS stress responses to nitrogen fixation. The findings demonstrate how stress signaling integrates symbiotic nitrogen fixation with host-microbe coordination.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Two transcription factors (MtERF82 and MtDOF5:53) maintain indeterminate nodule meristem",
    "Stage- and zone-specific expression of host and rhizobial genes along nodule axes",
    "ROS stress responses in host and rhizobia are critical for nitrogen fixation"
  ],
  "study_type": "spatial transcriptomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a spatiotemporal framework for understanding host-microbe coordination in nitrogen fixation, highlighting stress signaling as a conserved mechanism for symbiotic nitrogen fixation."
}
